@startuml domain-programme
' Report §2.4 — Programme bounded context in full. The classes come from
' include/domain-programme.iuml, the same source the overview (domain-model.puml) uses.
!pragma layout smetana
!include include/style.iuml
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members

title Programme context (event-catalog-service) — domain model

!include include/domain-programme.iuml
!include include/domain-published-language.iuml
!$only = "programme"
!include include/domain-event-links.iuml

' Show only the events this context touches, by name.
remove @unlinked
hide <<DomainEvent>> members

note top of Event
  <b>Invariants</b>
  · sessions are added only while DRAFT
  · a session's slot falls inside dateRange
  · publish() needs at least one session
    and is allowed only from DRAFT
  · capacity may change unless CANCELLED
end note

note bottom of SessionSchedulingPolicy
  Checks the candidate slot against every session in
  the catalogue: a speaker may not be booked for two
  overlapping slots. Called by EventApplicationService
  before Event.addSession(...).
end note

legend right
  Value objects are Java records, mapped as
  JPA @Embeddable. Session is inside the Event
  aggregate (cascade ALL, orphanRemoval).
  Speaker is a separate aggregate referenced
  only by id. EventStatus.CANCELLED exists, but
  no use case on main sets it.
endlegend
@enduml
